  "path": "README.md",
  "content": "# \ud83c\udf99\ufe0f Voice Agent\n\nA conversational AI assistant that can **talk to you** and help control your computer using voice commands.\n\n## Features\n\n\u2705 **Voice Input/Output** - Speak naturally to the agent\n\u2705 **AI Conversations** - Powered by OpenAI's GPT-4\n\u2705 **Web Search Integration** - Find information online\n\u2705 **File Operations** - Read, write, and organize files\n\u2705 **System Control** - Run applications and scripts\n\u2705 **Conversation Memory** - Remembers context across messages\n\u2705 **Text Fallback** - Type instead if microphone unavailable\n\n## Quick Start\n\n### 1. Clone/Setup\n\n```bash\n# Navigate to the voice agent directory\ncd voice_agent\n\n# Install dependencies\npip install -r requirements.txt\n```\n\n### 2. Get API Keys\n\nRun the interactive setup:\n\n```bash\npython setup_agent.py\n```\n\nThis will guide you through:\n- Getting an **OpenAI API key** (required)\n- Getting a **Google API key** (optional)\n- Checking dependencies\n- Saving configuration\n\n**OpenAI API Key:**\n- Visit: https://platform.openai.com/api-keys\n- Create a new secret key\n- The setup script will ask you to paste it\n\n### 3. Run the Agent\n\n```bash\npython voice_agent.py\n```\n\nThe agent will start and greet you. Then:\n- **Option 1**: Speak your message into the microphone\n- **Option 2**: Type your message\n- **Option 3**: Type 'quit' to exit\n\n## Configuration\n\nEdit `config.py` to customize:\n\n```python\nLLM_MODEL = \"gpt-4\"              # or \"gpt-3.5-turbo\" (cheaper)\nVOICE_RATE = 150                 # 100-300 words per minute\nMAX_RECORDING_DURATION = 10      # Max seconds per recording\nLLM_TEMPERATURE = 0.7            # 0.0-1.0 (higher = more creative)\n```\n\n## Architecture\n\n```\nvoice_agent/\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 voice_agent.py       # Main agent class\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 setup_agent.py       # Configuration wizard\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 config.py            # Settings and constants\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 requirements.txt     # Python dependencies\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 .env                 # API keys (created by setup)\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 logs/                # Agent logs\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 agent_data/          # Conversation history & memory\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 README.md            # This file\n```\n\n### Core Components\n\n**VoiceAgent Class:**\n- `__init__()` - Initialize with OpenAI API\n- `listen()` - Record audio and transcribe with Whisper\n- `speak()` - Convert text to speech with pyttsx3\n- `process_message()` - Send to GPT-4 and get response\n- `run()` - Main event loop\n\n## Usage Examples\n\n### Basic Conversation\n```\nYou: What's the weather today?\nAgent: I don't have real-time weather data, but I can help you search for it...\n```\n\n### File Operations\n```\nYou: Read the file called report.txt\nAgent: [reads and summarizes the file]\n```\n\n### Web Search\n```\nYou: Search for Python best practices\nAgent: [summarizes search results]\n```\n\n### System Commands\n```\nYou: Open Notepad\nAgent: [launches Notepad]\n```\n\n## Requirements\n\n### Hardware\n- Microphone (for voice input)\n- Speaker (for voice output)\n\n### Software\n- Python 3.8+\n- OpenAI API account (free tier available)\n- ffmpeg (for advanced audio recording)\n\n### Python Libraries\nSee `requirements.txt`\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### \"OPENAI_API_KEY not set\"\n\u2192 Run `python setup_agent.py` to configure your API key\n\n### \"No module named 'pyaudio'\"\n\u2192 Windows: `pip install pipwin` \u2192 `pipwin install pyaudio`\n\u2192 Mac: `brew install portaudio` \u2192 `pip install pyaudio`\n\u2192 Linux: `sudo apt-get install portaudio19-dev` \u2192 `pip install pyaudio`\n\n### Microphone not working\n\u2192 Check system audio settings\n\u2192 Try text input mode instead (Option 2)\n\u2192 Ensure microphone is not muted\n\n### Speech synthesis not working\n\u2192 Check speaker volume\n\u2192 Try another TTS voice: `pyttsx3.voice_ID` in `voice_agent.py`\n\n### Slow responses\n\u2192 Use `gpt-3.5-turbo` instead of `gpt-4` in `config.py` (faster, cheaper)\n\n## API Costs\n\n**OpenAI Usage:**\n- **Whisper** (speech-to-text): $0.02 per minute\n- **GPT-4** (text generation): $0.03 per 1K input tokens\n- **TTS** (text-to-speech): Handled locally by pyttsx3 (free)\n\n**Rough costs:**\n- 1 minute of conversation \u2248 $0.10-0.20\n- Use `gpt-3.5-turbo` to reduce costs 10x\n\n**Free tier options:**\n- OpenAI provides $5 free credits\n- Set up billing alerts to monitor costs\n\n## Advanced Features\n\n### Multi-turn Conversations\nThe agent maintains conversation history automatically. Context is preserved across messages.\n\n### Memory & Persistence\n- Conversation logs saved to `agent_data/conversations.json`\n- User preferences in `agent_data/memory.json`\n- Logs in `logs/voice_agent.log`\n\n### Custom System Prompt\nEdit the `system_prompt` in `VoiceAgent.__init__()` to change behavior.\n\n## Security\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f **Important:**\n1. **Never commit `.env` file** - It contains API keys!\n2. **Add to `.gitignore`** - Setup script does this automatically\n3. **Use environment variables** - Don't hardcode API keys\n4. **Regenerate keys** - If accidentally exposed, regenerate immediately\n5. **Monitor usage** - Check your OpenAI dashboard for unexpected charges\n\n## License\n\nThis project is provided as-is for educational purposes.\n\n## Support\n\nFor issues:\n1. Check the troubleshooting section\n2. Review logs in `logs/voice_agent.log`\n3. Check OpenAI API documentation: https://platform.openai.com/docs\n4. Search GitHub issues for similar problems\n\n## Next Steps\n\n1. **Run setup**: `python setup_agent.py`\n2. **Start agent**: `python voice_agent.py`\n3. **Enjoy**: Talk to your voice assistant! \ud83c\udf99\ufe0f\n\n---\n\nMade with \u2764\ufe0f for conversational AI enthusiasts\n"
}
