  "path": "GUIDE.md",
  "content": "# \ud83c\udf99\ufe0f Voice Agent - Complete Guide\n\n## Table of Contents\n1. [Quick Start](#quick-start)\n2. [Getting API Keys](#getting-api-keys)\n3. [Installation](#installation)\n4. [Running the Agent](#running-the-agent)\n5. [Features & Usage](#features--usage)\n6. [Troubleshooting](#troubleshooting)\n7. [Advanced Configuration](#advanced-configuration)\n\n---\n\n## Quick Start\n\n### 30-Second Setup\n\n```bash\n# 1. Install dependencies\npip install -r requirements.txt\n\n# 2. Run setup wizard\npython setup_agent.py\n\n# 3. Start the agent\npython voice_agent.py\n```\n\nThat's it! The agent will guide you from there.\n\n---\n\n## Getting API Keys\n\n### OpenAI API Key (Required)\n\n**Why you need it:**\n- Speech Recognition (Whisper)\n- Chat AI (GPT-4)\n- Text-to-Speech\n\n**How to get it:**\n\n1. Go to: **https://platform.openai.com/api-keys**\n2. Sign up or log in (it's free!)\n3. Click **\"Create new secret key\"**\n4. A key will appear (starts with `sk-`)\n5. **Copy it immediately** (you can't see it again!)\n6. Paste into the setup wizard when prompted\n\n**Cost information:**\n- Free trial: $5 credit (usually lasts 3 months)\n- After that: pay-as-you-go\n- Roughly $0.10-0.20 per minute of conversation\n- Use `gpt-3.5-turbo` in `config.py` to reduce costs 10x\n\n**Keep it safe:**\n- \u274c Don't commit to Git\n- \u274c Don't share with anyone\n- \u2705 Setup script adds `.env` to `.gitignore` automatically\n\n---\n\n## Installation\n\n### Prerequisites\n\n- **Python 3.8+** (check with `python --version`)\n- **Pip** (usually comes with Python)\n- **Microphone** (optional, can type instead)\n- **Speaker** (optional, can read text instead)\n\n### Step-by-Step\n\n**1. Navigate to the directory:**\n```bash\ncd voice_agent\n```\n\n**2. Create a virtual environment (optional but recommended):**\n```bash\n# Windows\npython -m venv venv\nvenv\\Scripts\\activate\n\n# Mac/Linux\npython3 -m venv venv\nsource venv/bin/activate\n```\n\n**3. Install dependencies:**\n```bash\npip install -r requirements.txt\n```\n\n**4. Run setup:**\n```bash\npython setup_agent.py\n```\n\nThe setup wizard will:\n- Ask for your OpenAI API key\n- Check that all dependencies are installed\n- Create a `.env` file with your configuration\n- Update `.gitignore` for security\n\n---\n\n## Running the Agent\n\n### Basic Voice Agent\n\n```bash\npython voice_agent.py\n```\n\n**What it does:**\n- Listens to voice input (via microphone)\n- Converts speech to text (Whisper)\n- Processes with GPT-4\n- Converts response back to speech\n- Plays the audio to you\n\n**Interaction modes:**\n- **Option 1**: Voice input - Speak into the microphone\n- **Option 2**: Text input - Type your message\n- **Option 3**: Quit - Type 'exit' or 'quit'\n\n### Advanced Voice Agent\n\n```bash\npython voice_agent_advanced.py\n```\n\n**Extra features:**\n- \ud83d\udd0d Web search integration\n- \ud83d\udcc2 File operations (read/write)\n- \ud83d\udcbe Conversation memory\n- \ud83d\udcca Conversation logs\n\n---\n\n## Features & Usage\n\n### Feature 1: Voice Conversation\n\n**How it works:**\n1. Agent greets you\n2. You choose input mode (voice/text)\n3. Agent processes and responds\n4. Response is spoken aloud\n5. Repeat!\n\n**Example:**\n```\nYou: What is machine learning?\nAgent: Machine learning is a subset of artificial intelligence where...\n[Agent speaks the response]\n```\n\n### Feature 2: Web Search (Advanced Agent Only)\n\n**Trigger words:**\n- \"Search for...\"\n- \"Look up...\"\n- \"Find...\"\n- \"What is...\"\n\n**Example:**\n```\nYou: Search for latest AI news\nAgent: [Performs web search and summarizes]\n```\n\n### Feature 3: File Operations (Advanced Agent Only)\n\n**Supported operations:**\n\n**Read a file:**\n```\nYou: Read file document.txt\nAgent: [Reads and displays file content]\n```\n\n**List files:**\n```\nYou: List files\nAgent: [Shows files in current directory]\n```\n\n**Write a file:**\n```\nYou: Write to file notes.txt \"Remember to call John\"\nAgent: [Writes content to file]\n```\n\n### Feature 4: Conversation Memory\n\n**What's saved:**\n- Your conversation history\n- Context from previous messages\n- User preferences\n- Session timestamps\n\n**Where it's saved:**\n- `agent_data/conversations.json` - Full conversation log\n- `agent_data/memory.json` - Agent memory\n\n**Privacy:**\n- All data stored locally\n- Not sent to OpenAI\n- You can delete anytime\n\n---\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Problem: \"OPENAI_API_KEY not set\"\n\n**Solution:**\n```bash\npython setup_agent.py\n```\n\nThen paste your API key when prompted.\n\n---\n\n### Problem: \"No module named 'pyaudio'\"\n\n**Windows:**\n```bash\npip install pipwin\npipwin install pyaudio\n```\n\n**Mac:**\n```bash\nbrew install portaudio\npip install pyaudio\n```\n\n**Linux:**\n```bash\nsudo apt-get install portaudio19-dev\npip install pyaudio\n```\n\n---\n\n### Problem: \"Microphone not working\"\n\n**Checklist:**\n1. \u2713 Microphone is plugged in\n2. \u2713 Microphone is not muted\n3. \u2713 Volume is up in Windows Settings\n4. \u2713 No other app is using the microphone\n\n**Workaround:**\nUse text input instead (Option 2 when prompted)\n\n---\n\n### Problem: \"Speaker not playing audio\"\n\n**Checklist:**\n1. \u2713 Speaker is plugged in / volume is up\n2. \u2713 Windows volume is not muted\n3. \u2713 Audio driver is installed\n\n**Test:**\n```bash\npython -c \"import pyttsx3; pyttsx3.init().say('test'); pyttsx3.init().runAndWait()\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Problem: \"Slow responses / Timeout errors\"\n\n**Solution 1:** Use cheaper model\n```python\n# In config.py, change:\nLLM_MODEL = \"gpt-3.5-turbo\"  # Faster and cheaper\n```\n\n**Solution 2:** Check internet connection\n```bash\nping google.com\n```\n\n**Solution 3:** Check OpenAI API status\nVisit: https://status.openai.com\n\n---\n\n### Problem: \"Expensive API calls\"\n\n**Solutions:**\n1. Use `gpt-3.5-turbo` instead of `gpt-4` (10x cheaper)\n2. Keep conversations shorter\n3. Set up billing alerts in OpenAI dashboard\n\n---\n\n## Advanced Configuration\n\n### Customize the Agent\n\nEdit `config.py`:\n\n```python\n# Model choice\nLLM_MODEL = \"gpt-3.5-turbo\"  # Cheaper, 10x faster\n# LLM_MODEL = \"gpt-4\"         # More powerful, expensive\n\n# Voice settings\nVOICE_RATE = 150             # 100-300 words per minute\nVOICE_VOLUME = 0.9           # 0.0-1.0\n\n# Recording settings\nMAX_RECORDING_DURATION = 10  # Seconds\nSILENCE_THRESHOLD = 0.01     # For auto-stop\n\n# Response settings\nLLM_TEMPERATURE = 0.7        # 0.0 (factual) to 1.0 (creative)\nLLM_MAX_TOKENS = 500         # Max response length\n```\n\n### Change Agent Behavior\n\nEdit the `system_prompt` in `voice_agent.py`:\n\n```python\nself.system_prompt = \"\"\"You are a helpful assistant that...\n[Your custom instructions here]\n\"\"\"\n```\n\n### Enable/Disable Features\n\nIn `config.py`:\n\n```python\nENABLE_WEB_SEARCH = True\nENABLE_FILE_OPERATIONS = True\nENABLE_SYSTEM_CONTROL = True\nENABLE_MEMORY = True\n```\n\n### Use a Different Voice\n\nIn `voice_agent.py`:\n\n```python\n# List available voices\nvoices = self.tts_engine.getProperty('voices')\nfor voice in voices:\n    print(voice.id)\n\n# Set a specific voice\nself.tts_engine.setProperty('voice', voices[1].id)  # Try index 0, 1, 2, etc.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Performance Tips\n\n### Faster Responses\n1. Use `gpt-3.5-turbo` instead of `gpt-4`\n2. Reduce `LLM_MAX_TOKENS` (default 500)\n3. Use text input instead of voice\n\n### Lower API Costs\n1. Use `gpt-3.5-turbo` (10x cheaper)\n2. Keep conversations short\n3. Batch similar questions together\n\n### Better Voice Quality\n1. Increase `VOICE_RATE` for faster speech\n2. Try different voices (see config above)\n3. Test microphone quality\n\n---\n\n## Security Best Practices\n\n### Protecting Your API Key\n\n1. **Never commit `.env` to Git**\n   ```bash\n   # Already done by setup script, but verify:\n   cat .gitignore | grep \".env\"\n   ```\n\n2. **Don't share your .env file**\n   ```bash\n   # Even if you delete it from Git, it might be in history:\n   git filter-branch --force --index-filter \\\n     'git rm --cached --ignore-unmatch .env' \\\n     --prune-empty --tag-name-filter cat -- --all\n   ```\n\n3. **Regenerate if exposed**\n   - Go to https://platform.openai.com/api-keys\n   - Delete the old key\n   - Create a new key\n   - Update your `.env` file\n\n4. **Monitor usage**\n   - Check your OpenAI dashboard regularly\n   - Set billing alerts\n   - Report unusual usage\n\n---\n\n## Logs & Debugging\n\n### Where logs are saved\n```\nvoice_agent/logs/voice_agent.log\n```\n\n### View logs\n```bash\n# Windows\ntype logs\\voice_agent.log\n\n# Mac/Linux\ncat logs/voice_agent.log\n\n# Real-time tail\ntail -f logs/voice_agent.log\n```\n\n### Enable debug mode\nEdit `voice_agent.py` and change:\n```python\nDEBUG = True  # Prints more info\n```\n\n---\n\n## Advanced: Creating Custom Skills\n\nAdd new capabilities to the agent:\n\n```python\n# In voice_agent.py, add a new method:\n\ndef calculate(self, expression: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Custom skill: Calculate math expressions\"\"\"\n    try:\n        result = eval(expression)\n        return f\"The answer is {result}\"\n    except:\n        return \"Invalid expression\"\n```\n\nThen update `execute_action()` to trigger it:\n\n```python\nif \"calculate\" in message_lower:\n    expression = user_message.replace(\"calculate\", \"\").strip()\n    return self.calculate(expression)\n```\n\n---\n\n## FAQ\n\n**Q: Is my voice data sent to OpenAI?**\nA: Only the audio files for transcription. Use `gpt-3.5-turbo` or local speech-to-text to avoid this.\n\n**Q: Can I use this offline?**\nA: No, it requires internet for OpenAI APIs. Consider using local LLMs for offline use.\n\n**Q: Can I run multiple agents?**\nA: Yes, but each will consume API quota. Run them sequentially to avoid conflicts.\n\n**Q: How do I update the agent?**\nA: Pull latest files from your repository or manually update the code.\n\n**Q: Can I add more features?**\nA: Yes! The agent is fully customizable. See \"Advanced: Creating Custom Skills\" above.\n\n---\n\n## Getting Help\n\n1. **Check logs**: `logs/voice_agent.log`\n2. **Review errors**: Error messages usually explain the problem\n3. **Test dependencies**: `python setup_agent.py`\n4. **Check OpenAI status**: https://status.openai.com\n5. **Read OpenAI docs**: https://platform.openai.com/docs\n\n---\n\n## Next Steps\n\n1. \u2705 Run `python setup_agent.py`\n2. \u2705 Paste your OpenAI API key\n3. \u2705 Run `python voice_agent.py`\n4. \u2705 Start talking! \ud83c\udf99\ufe0f\n\nEnjoy your voice assistant! \ud83d\ude80\n"
}
